Avery, Priya,

Thank you both for Wednesday. It was the most useful hour I have spent with a company this quarter, and I don't say that to be polite. Priya, the way you drew the ingest path and then crossed out the half of it that customers never see was exactly the level I needed.

Where I've landed, for transparency: Larkspur is interested. Our partners meet on the first Tuesday of each month and I would like to bring Tessera to the April meeting with a real view rather than an impression. To do that I need to understand the expansion motion in numbers, not anecdotes. You mentioned that the plants which added a second line did so within two quarters, and that the 2024 cohort behaves differently from 2025. That is the thing my partners will push on.

So, my one pointed question: by cohort of plants (grouped by the quarter they went live), how many have added a second line, how quickly, and what did that do to the contract value? Whatever form you already keep it in is fine; I am not asking for a new analysis, only the data behind the sentence you said on Wednesday.

